  "statement": "Find the sum to $n$ terms of the series $1+2x+3x^{2}+\\cdots+nx^{n-1}$ for $x\\neq1$.",
  "solution": "Let $S_{n}=1+2x+3x^{2}+\\cdots+nx^{n-1}$. Multiply by $x$: $xS_{n}=x+2x^{2}+3x^{3}+\\cdots+nx^{n}$. Subtracting, $(1-x)S_{n}=1+x+x^{2}+\\cdots+x^{n-1}-nx^{n}=\\frac{1-x^{n}}{1-x}-nx^{n}$. Hence $S_{n}=\\frac{1-x^{n}}{(1-x)^{2}}-\\frac{nx^{n}}{1-x}$.",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
